--- the rows after the last growth take the join over the spill threshold
right_halved: the same result, spilled 0, switched 0, halved 1
full_halved: the same result, spilled 0, switched 0, halved 1
anti_halved: the same result, spilled 0, switched 0, halved 1
packed_string_halved: the same result, spilled 0, switched 0, halved 1
string_halved: the same result, spilled 0, switched 0, halved 1
--- a growth step would take the join over the spill threshold
right_switched: the same result, spilled 0, switched 1, halved 0
full_switched: the same result, spilled 0, switched 1, halved 0
anti_switched: the same result, spilled 0, switched 1, halved 0
packed_string_switched: the same result, spilled 0, switched 1, halved 0
string_switched: the same result, spilled 0, switched 1, halved 0
--- two disjuncts, so two hash tables that grow together, at a memory limit of 0.75 of the peak memory
or: the same result, spilled 0, switched 1, halved 0
--- two disjuncts, one with 10 keys, at a memory limit of 1.25 of the peak memory
or_few_keys: the same result, spilled 0, switched 0, halved 0
